  // design: St. John's step 6 (PLAN 3.2 D, Welles's mess hall): the room is the two cells of the bay with no wall between them (16 m across, 8 m along), so bays end to end make one long hall; the hall's ends are what it meets (a Stair End Bay's mouth). The long walls are a choice (option Long walls): arched windows (the default), a round-arched way in on one side or both, or a solid wall with the fireplace (a cold hearth of blocks: nothing burns, glows or flickers). The piers stand at the bay's west end, so a row of bays has one every 8 m. Step 7a: Main entrance north / south (the Twin arches wall style, format v49) is the hall's door from outside, two arches on a middle pier; the south banner hangs only where the south wall is not that entrance (a `when` list). The plan's floor sunk half a metre is not built (MapMaker's sunken centre is refused on the ground: no room under it); the hall is the level's 3.5 m.
  // step7d: St. John's step 7d (the owner's sketch and photos 6 and 7, OWNER_NOTES_2026-11-21). Every new option's first choice is the bay as it was, so placements made before keep their look. Floor Sunk 0.5 m: the tiles are Sunk Rooms (core.room_sunk: the slab half a metre down, the ground cut out of the cell), a footing 0.6 m wide under each long wall whose top is the doorways' threshold, one step of 0.25 m, half a metre deep, inside every doorway (4 m wide at a round arch, 7 m at the twin arches), the wall piers and the long walls' fireplaces on feet; furniture stands half a metre lower (each floor-standing part is listed for both floors). Ceiling Timber beams: kit.roof.timber_bay under the ceiling (beams over the bay's ends and its middle: over the arcade's piers). Side aisle Arcade south: kit.wall.arcade along z = 0 (half a pier at each end of the bay and a whole one in its middle, arches 3 m: a round-arched south door faces the middle pier, the twin arches face the two arches), its foot 0.45 m under the floor so one model serves both floors; the aisle is 3.1 m deep, the main hall 11.1 m. Furniture Rows (and Rows with a podium: a kit.table.lectern and a kit.monument.bell_stand against the north wall): kit.table.mess, four rows at z 1.85, 4.66, 7.47 and 10.28, evenly spaced as the photographs show them, with three aisles of 2.05 m between them (what bots need; the middle one is on the fireplace), 1.07 m between the first row and the arcade and the last row's chairs by the north wall's piers: bots keep to those aisles and reach the side aisle only through a bay whose aisle has no small tables (one with a way in on its south side, by its cross aisle), players walk in anywhere; two tables a row; the west table of each row is left out unless the West end is Open. Rows with a cross aisle: kit.table.mess_small at each end of the bay. The aisle's small tables stand only where the south wall has no way in. West end: Steps up is one step across the end between the footings; the end walls are blocks (0.45 m, a hair under the ceiling); the fireplace wall is kit.wall.fireplace between two kit.wall.panel_window, centred on the main hall (z 5.95 with the arcade, 4 without), scaled 0.96 on a level floor to stand under a 3.5 m ceiling, with one steady light at the hearth. Parts under the level's floor: map/setPieceCheck.ts allows a part up to 1 m under the piece's lowest floor.
  // piers: Owner, 2026-11-22 (the reference photos: a square limestone pier with a plain capital under each beam on the window side). Ceiling Timber beams on piers: on the north side half a pier at each end of the bay (two bays make a whole one, 1 m wide) and a whole one in the middle, 0.45 m deep (the old wall pier's face, so the aisles and the north row's chairs are where they were), each with a capital block under the beam at 3.06 m; blocks in the walls' own stone (no new model). A pier under the middle beam stands where the bay's one arched window is, so with this choice the north wall's window is the Twin sash windows (one either side of the middle pier); a bay with a way in or a fireplace in its north wall has no middle pier. The old north wall pier is left out; the south side is as it was (the arcade's piers are there, or the old wall pier).
