  // design: St. John's step 8b (Memorial Hall, the library, to the owner's direction: two storeys, alcoves on the ground floor as in one interior photo, rows upstairs under the open roof as in the other; docs/map-briefs/st_johns, OWNER_NOTES_2026-11-21). Ground storey: two Rooms open to each other and at both ends, fieldstone walls (the stone role), a ceiling of pale plaster (the upper floor's underside) with three dark beams across it; four Bookcase Presses standing out 3 m from the long walls, 4 m apart, each with its bench and reading ledge in the alcove west of it; a square Leaded Window in the middle alcove of each wall, its sill 1 m up; a Worn Rug and the Globe in the middle (4.5 m of floor either side of it); two Hanging Lanterns. Upper storey: two Rooms with no roof (ceiling Open), their walls hung with tiles as shingles (Clay Roof Tiles, tinted; a wall of one material shows it on both faces, so inside a pale plaster lining 2.35 m high stands against each, up to the windows' sills); the Ridge Roof Bay over them at the walls' top (its foot 1.8 m under it), two trusses a bay; four Double-sided Bookcases in two rows either side of a 4 m aisle with the Carpet Runner down it (2.3 m of floor between a row and its wall); two wide Leaded Windows a wall, tight under the eaves and close together; two lanterns hung from the trusses. Arch porch (the owner's exterior photo: the arch stands in the ground storey's own wall, the upper storey and its windows run on above it, the porch is a recess into the building): that wall's side is left open and built as blocks stepped behind the Parabolic Stone Arch's band (the opening 4.5 m wide at the ground, 3.15 m at the crown), the game's own crest on the crown; behind it Dark Wood Panels close a porch 6 m wide and 3 m deep with a 2 m doorway on into the library; that wall's two presses and its window are left out. Lights: two, and one in the porch. The roof collides as nothing: nobody reaches it, a grenade thrown high leaves through it.
