  // design: St. John's step 8b (the owner: two levels, spiral stairs to go up and down; docs/map-briefs/st_johns). The Library Bay (two storeys)'s west end: the Spiral Stair tile in the south cell, its shaft against the south wall and its doors north on both floors (its own sides left open: the outer walls there are four blocks, fieldstone below and shingles above, since a two-level tile's walls are one material), a Room north of it on each storey with walls north and west; the Ridge Roof Bay's end variant (its gable over the west wall). Ground: two Bookcase Presses on the north wall, square Leaded Windows north, west (two) and south (two, in the wall behind the stair's drum: they show outside only), a rug before the stair's door, a lantern. Upstairs: two Double-sided Bookcases along the north side, the runner, wide Leaded Windows in pairs north, south and west, two lanterns; the game's own crest (the Crest Shield) on the east truss's collar, facing the hall. Turns only (the stair is not its own mirror image). Two lights. Blocks 4.
